      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac4{2+\\sqrt5}&=\\frac{4(2-\\sqrt5)}{4-5}\\\\\\frac4{2+\\sqrt5}&=-8+4\\sqrt5\\\\\\frac1{9-4\\sqrt5}&=\\frac{9+4\\sqrt5}{81-80}\\\\\\frac1{9-4\\sqrt5}&=9+4\\sqrt5\\\\\\frac4{2+\\sqrt5}-\\frac1{9-4\\sqrt5}&=(-8+4\\sqrt5)-(9+4\\sqrt5)\\\\\\frac4{2+\\sqrt5}-\\frac1{9-4\\sqrt5}&=-17\\end{align*}$$\nSince $-17$ is an integer, the expression is rational.",
